🎛️
"Instruments"/en
=== start/en
¶The same eight bars, played by every instrument in the palette. Choose a name
and the melody keeps its place — only the voice changes.

Most of these are real recordings. The three synthesizers are not imitating
anything: they are synthesizers, and that is the sound.¶

¶Which instrument the melody is playing. Choice() gives back the name of
whatever selectable output was picked, and ø until something is.¶
picked: Choice()

¶One entry per instrument: what to call it, what plays it, and the colour its
button takes.¶
•Voice(label•'' icon•'' sound•🔈 hue•#°)

voices•[Voice]: [
	Voice('piano' '🎹' 🔈.🎹 260°)
	Voice('guitar' '🎸' 🔈.🎸 20°)
	Voice('violin' '🎻' 🔈.🎻 40°)
	Voice('flute' '🪈' 🔈.🪈 180°)
	Voice('trumpet' '🎺' 🔈.🎺 50°)
	Voice('sax' '🎷' 🔈.🎷 70°)
	Voice('bell' '🔔' 🔈.🔔 55°)
	Voice('drums' '🥁' 🔈.🥁 0°)
	Voice('didgeridoo' '🎶' 🔈.didgeridoo 15°)
	Voice('cat' '🐱' 🔈.🐱 330°)
	Voice('dog' '🐶' 🔈.🐶 35°)
	Voice('synth' '🎛️' 🔈.🎛️ 290°)
	Voice('bass' '🎛️' 🔈.synthBass 310°)
	Voice('pad' '🎛️' 🔈.synthPad 200°)
]

¶The chosen voice, or the piano before anyone has chosen. find() gives back ø
when nothing matches, so the fallback has to be a Voice of its own.¶
chosen: voices.find(ƒ(voice•Voice) voice.label = picked)
current•Voice: chosen•ø ? Voice('piano' '🎹' 🔈.🎹 260°) chosen

¶A melody that stays put while the instrument underneath it changes. Degrees,
not notes, so it means the same thing on every instrument — and on the drums
it reads as rhythm instead, since degrees index the kit there.¶
tune: [1 3 5 6 5 3 2 ø]

¶One button per instrument: the icon stacked above its name, so they don't
run into each other. Selectable phrases are what Choice() reads, and the
current one is drawn brighter so you can see where you are.¶
ƒ button(voice•Voice)
	Group(
		Stack(padding: 0.1m)
		[
			Phrase(voice.icon 1.1m)
			Phrase(voice.label 0.5m)
		]
		name: voice.label
		selectable: ⊤
		color: (voice.label = current.label)
			? Color(95% 60 voice.hue)
			Color(60% 8 voice.hue)
	)

¶Everything visible goes in one Stack. A Stage centres each of its children
on its own, so left loose they would all sit on top of each other — the
layout has to say they go one above the next.¶
🎭(
	[
		🔳(
			Stack(padding: 0.6m)
			[
				💬(current.icon 2.5m)
				💬(current.label 1.2m)
				🔳(
					Row(padding: 0.4m)
					voices.translate(ƒ(voice•Voice) button(voice))
				)
			]
		)
		🎼(
			🎶(tune instrument: current.sound)
			tempo: 120beats/min
			scale: 🎼.pentatonic
			name: current.label
		)
	]
	background: Color(14% 12 280°)
	color: Color(95% 0 0°)
)
